Credit: xLights
===============

PixelFlow is an independent project. It was inspired by xLights, the sequencer
the holiday lighting community has built and relied on for many years, and it
can import xLights shows and sequences. It is not xLights and is not affiliated
with or endorsed by the xLights project. Its design, its engine, and most of
its code are its own.

Some parts of PixelFlow are derived from xLights' source code, and are not only
inspired by it. They are: a number of the renderer's effects; rules every layer
passes through, such as blending, blur, and line drawing; the model geometry
that puts each pixel of a prop where xLights puts it, for imported props and
for several of PixelFlow's own shapes; value curves; and tables of defaults,
ranges, and shapes. Those parts are used under xLights'
licence, the GNU General Public License, version 3, and that is why PixelFlow
as a whole is offered under the same licence.

    xLights
    https://github.com/xLightsSequencer/xLights
    Copyright (C) the xLights authors and contributors
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3

The file-by-file record of what is derived, with the xLights file each one
follows, is docs/licensing/provenance.md in PixelFlow's source. Each of those
files also names the xLights file it follows in its opening comment.

Thank you to everyone who has written and maintained xLights. PixelFlow could
not have been made without their work.

The list gets shorter over time. Where PixelFlow can do a part better with a
design of its own, that part is rewritten from a description of what it shows
and moves out of the derived list: Pinwheel and Shockwave so far. The rest
stays, credited here.


